{
 "about": "Sentences a person might say or type to a calculator, and the fields they mean. Forms are copied from the live pages named in `source` (labels, ids, ranges, choices). Scored by assistant.test.mjs; the Ask page prints the score the build measured. A case passes only if every expected field gets exactly the expected value and nothing else is written. Add a case whenever a real sentence fails: the score is only worth what the cases are. Cases marked `tuned` were written alongside the rules and pass by construction; `held-out` cases were written afterwards and scored without changing the rules to fit them, so their score is the honest estimate.",
